WEBVTT

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:19.740
Bondo, if it's too hard...

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.820
No, I'll do it.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.110
Hey, Bondo!

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:41.080
Get a hold of yourself!

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:42.500
Bondo!

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:44.120
Kotarou!

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:21.160
Bondo, we reached town.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.410
Episode 20
"Moving On From a Standstill"

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:23.040
Luis?

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.240
Okay.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.530
Put these away, newbie.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:42.480
Don't get cocky, you yellow monkey. 
You don't even have a useful ability.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.930
Next time you pull this crap, I'll kill you.

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:55.220
I'll help.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:57.960
Oh...

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:00.320
Thanks, Luis.

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:07.330
Cheap meat is tough,

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:09.410
but it has a unique taste.

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:10.580
Right, Bondo?

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:12.220
We have another mission tomorrow.

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:13.750
Eat up.

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:15.410
Yeah.

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:36.440
I...

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:37.560
I...

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:38.940
I...

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:42.130
I killed...

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:45.220
I killed a...

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:48.580
I... I...

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:51.330
I... I...

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.210
Kotarou.

00:03:58.570 --> 00:03:59.710
Yasmin?

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:02.220
No dying.

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:15.060
<i>Guardian had several fronts,</i>

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:17.290
<i>one of them being a private security firm.</i>

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:20.190
<i>Basically, it was a mercenary 
group comprised of superhumans.</i>

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:23.840
<i>In the six months after I 
practically fled from Japan,</i>

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:25.820
<i>I experienced a lot of firsts.</i>

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:27.510
<i>My first war zone.</i>

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:29.830
<i>My first sight of real poverty.</i>

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:34.830
<i>My first time feeling the bloodlust 
of a real, live human.</i>

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.090
Get these done too, newbie.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.540
But you should maintain your own guns...

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:54.600
Monkeys shouldn't speak.

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:59.720
<i>But the superhuman tendency to discriminate 
against those with inferior abilities</i>

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:01.510
<i>was the same everywhere, I found.</i>

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:05.510
Sheesh. Leaving their weapons 
in the hands of others?

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:08.120
Don't know if they're ballsy or stupid.

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:11.370
I'll help once this is done.

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:13.730
Luis, uh...

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:15.000
Sorry about last night.

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:17.710
It doesn't bother me.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:19.520
In fact, I got to hog two meals.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:20.630
I'm very happy.

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:25.250
<i>There was one more first I 
experienced in this country:</i>

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:27.130
<i>having a true comrade-in-arms.</i>

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:36.130
Whoa, Midou.

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:37.390
Close one.

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:39.770
Damn, Bondo got me again!

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:41.520
Pincer attack, Tenjin!

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:42.900
You got it, Tenma!

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:44.900
No using hands!

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:46.180
Cheating!

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:47.400
Luis, pass!

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:48.640
Bring it!

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:52.910
<i>We often played with the local 
kids when we were off duty.</i>

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:57.290
<i>They were always smiling, even though 
they lived in a time of war and poverty.</i>

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.790
<i>Just watching those smiles 
offered me salva—</i>

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:11.600
Look, guys.

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:13.220
A spring in his shoe!

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:14.640
He's a cheater!

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:16.820
No fair, Bondo!

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:18.270
Get him, everyone!

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:19.900
Hey, wait!

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:21.670
Sorry!

00:06:21.670 --> 00:06:22.650
Spur of moment!

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:26.070
Sorry, sorry!

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:27.650
What are you guys doing to Bondo?!

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:29.110
Yasmin?

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:29.910
B-But...

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:31.780
I don't want to hear your excuses!

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:34.030
Crap! Yasmin's mad!

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:35.480
Yasmin...

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:37.360
Uh, saved me.

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:38.290
Thanks.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:40.920
<i>She's mad, all right.</i>

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:44.880
<i>Of course she is, after what I did.</i>

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:48.510
You only play with Midou and guys.

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:49.510
No fair.

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:54.760
Er, forgive with this.

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:58.560
Only this time.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:00.010
A chocolate bar!

00:07:00.010 --> 00:07:01.680
Why does only Yasmin get one?

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:02.560
Not fair!

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:04.920
I want one, too, Bondo!

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:06.940
Why are you joining in, Luis?

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:14.560
I don't get rationed a 
lot of sweets, y'know...

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:17.250
Halfsies.

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:18.230
You sure?

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:20.710
Thanks, then.

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:25.710
Life in this country's painful.

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:31.280
But we all halfsies the pain and live.

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:32.400
Yasmin...

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:35.720
Let's halfsies, Kotarou.

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:39.220
So good!

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:40.980
Y...

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:42.910
Yeah.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:50.860
Why did you come to this country, Kotarou?

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:53.360
I ran here.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:56.300
Lots of people say the same.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:58.300
They don't look it.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:01.760
They think they can stay 
strong while raising hell.

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:03.180
But they're scared and anxious.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:05.460
How about you? Why'd you come here?

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:07.790
I was in track and field since childhood.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:12.520
Was expected to represent my country 
in javelin and bring home a medal.

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:13.650
But then...

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:14.780
Men in black showed up?

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:16.990
Well, it's more money than a medal.

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:19.460
Not a bad deal for a poor guy like me.

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:20.580
Luis...

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:25.580
And what was your story?

00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:32.760
Bondo, are you tired?

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:34.440
No.

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:37.980
Your smiles fill me with energy.

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:39.450
Okay, then.

00:08:39.820 --> 00:08:42.600
Is school fun for you all?

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:45.700
Kids enjoy school lunch.

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:49.090
I'm learning programming on computer.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:51.060
That's good.

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:54.970
You said you want to learn 
programming before.

00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:59.720
I'll use computer to feed 
everyone lots of food.

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:01.470
You fighter.

00:09:02.210 --> 00:09:04.690
Thanks to person who donated it.

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:07.480
Kind people exist.

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:09.230
Really.

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:13.840
Bondo, join us!

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:14.990
Help out.

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:16.990
I can't beat them by myself.

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:18.620
Okay, let's do this.

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:20.620
<i>After running to this land,</i>

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:23.060
<i>I'd come to a standstill yet again.</i>

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:25.010
<i>While I did some good here and there,</i>

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:28.920
<i>that was but the price I paid to avert 
my eyes from my smoldering depression.</i>

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:30.130
<i>And, just like that,</i>

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:33.130
<i>I entered my second year 
of life as a mercenary.</i>

00:09:33.490 --> 00:09:38.010
The goal of this mission is to wipe out 
the forces stationed in the factory that's

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:40.760
manufacturing a new type of narcotic 
and blow the whole thing up.

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:44.020
Also, monsters have been spotted 
in the factory's vicinity.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:46.770
Can't we just carpet bomb the place?

00:09:46.990 --> 00:09:48.290
The problem is that

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:50.330
the factory is close to the border.

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:52.810
We don't want to wake up our neighbors.

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:54.650
What are those plots of land along the roads?

00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:56.050
Farms.

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:58.740
They're growing grains, which 
can provide handy cover.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:00.410
We'll sneak in from here.

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:04.290
Once you occupy the factory, confiscate 
the narcotics and their ingredients.

00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:07.160
If you find any Gaia fanatics, shoot to kill.

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:10.100
We're not capturing the summoners?

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:13.140
Kill a summoner, and his 
monsters stop moving.

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:15.210
We can support other teams that way.

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:17.170
Oh, I see.

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:18.520
Each team is to assign

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:21.840
the appropriate members and 
equipment for their roles.

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:22.680
Dismissed!

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:26.890
Luis, Bondo, come with me.

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:29.440
Team Variant is in charge
of the direct assault.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:30.370
Sir!

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:33.660
We've never had such a 
large-scale mission before.

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:35.930
Let's visit the school tomorrow.

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:37.480
Yeah, sounds good.

00:10:41.730 --> 00:10:43.170
Let's go, Kotarou.

00:10:43.170 --> 00:10:45.540
We can see them again after the mission.

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:47.560
Right.

00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:30.250
Split up into two groups 
and neutralize all enemies.

00:11:30.530 --> 00:11:31.370
Roger.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:09.080
Damn it!

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:09.620
What?

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:12.830
I've never seen a monster like that!

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:16.210
Crap—

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:19.870
Bondo!

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:27.760
We can't beat that.

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:28.920
Let's stop the summoner.

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:29.770
Got it.

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:33.560
Where could the summoner be?

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:35.780
He should be at a safe 
distance and have protection.

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:42.900
Bingo.

00:13:05.460 --> 00:13:06.630
No way.

00:13:14.990 --> 00:13:16.270
Yasmin?

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:17.900
Kotarou.

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:26.610
I didn't realize until I fired...

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:28.320
I shot them...

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:31.450
Class needs money.

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:37.490
We can all communicate with djinn.

00:13:37.490 --> 00:13:38.460
All of you?

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:42.820
You mean you tried to reduce 
the consumption of life force

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:47.040
by contracting with one 
large monster together?

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:49.050
W-Will you kill us?

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:54.180
Stay quiet.

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:57.480
<i>Four lightly wounded by stray bullets.</i>

00:13:57.480 --> 00:13:59.140
<i>Four dead.</i>

00:13:59.140 --> 00:14:00.190
<i>Two on the verge of death.</i>

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:03.190
<i>They can be saved if they 
receive immediate treatment.</i>

00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:05.690
I went and did it again...

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:08.700
You couldn't have known in that split second.

00:14:08.900 --> 00:14:11.340
They were so young!

00:14:11.340 --> 00:14:13.460
This is too awful!

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:24.130
This is Variant 4.

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:27.380
We've neutralized six summoners.

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:31.550
Captain!

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:33.430
What's with the glare?

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:37.180
Do you wish to say killing 
wounded kids is wrong?

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:38.070
Yes.

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:41.000
You useless punk.

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:42.770
We've taken over the factory.

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:44.610
We withdraw before dawn.

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:45.820
Yes, sir...

00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:55.240
Whatever you're trying to do, don't!

00:14:55.550 --> 00:14:59.440
I'm sure that ability you just tried 
to use eats away at your life.

00:14:59.890 --> 00:15:01.000
Don't use it.

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:04.540
I knew that those two would get killed.

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:06.010
But I still did it.

00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:08.630
That was the only way to 
save Yasmin and the rest.

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:11.260
Yeah, it was.

00:15:16.030 --> 00:15:17.210
Screw this...

00:15:18.090 --> 00:15:19.460
Screw it all!

00:15:20.460 --> 00:15:22.350
I won't accept Guardian's methods.

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:24.230
I will never accept

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:26.910
superhumans who discriminate against,

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:30.360
look down upon, and walk all over people.

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:31.550
Let's go.

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:32.990
I feel the same way.

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:39.000
This place will be bombed soon.

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:42.440
<i>The neighboring country was 
the narcotic factory's client.</i>

00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:46.250
<i>And they were going to carpet bomb 
the place to get rid of the evidence.</i>

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:49.260
Yasmin, if you can't run...

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:51.130
No! I'm okay!

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:52.760
Here it comes.

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:00.380
That's a glide missile.

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:03.340
It can turn a 300-meter 
area into a sea of flames.

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:06.520
It's only a matter of time until 
they start firing those here.

00:16:10.050 --> 00:16:11.780
Luis, what are you...

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:16.280
This is how I use these.

00:16:25.340 --> 00:16:26.330
He took it out.

00:16:26.990 --> 00:16:28.530
I'll defend the path of retreat.

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:31.340
Take the kids and go.

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:32.710
Go?

00:16:32.710 --> 00:16:33.970
What about you?

00:16:34.170 --> 00:16:36.720
I'll be right behind you 
once I secure the path.

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:39.720
Do as Luis says

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:39.720
Take Luis along

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:39.720
Stay here

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:40.560
Do as Luis says

00:16:41.030 --> 00:16:41.980
Got it.

00:16:43.400 --> 00:16:46.600
I once hit a friend of mine.

00:16:48.370 --> 00:16:49.970
It was a trivial fight.

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:53.150
But he died from it.

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:54.540
I see.

00:16:55.250 --> 00:16:58.120
I volunteered to come here to punish myself.

00:16:59.020 --> 00:17:01.390
But I've had enough of living this way.

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:04.500
I'm going to quit standing still.

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:10.630
I think I'll do that, too.

00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:12.270
I'm going ahead.

00:17:12.740 --> 00:17:13.630
I'll be waiting.

00:17:14.110 --> 00:17:14.880
Yeah.

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:20.760
Keep at it! We're almost there!

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:28.650
We made it...

00:17:30.870 --> 00:17:31.830
That's enough!

00:17:31.830 --> 00:17:32.900
Run, Luis!

00:17:41.690 --> 00:17:44.490
You can't do that, man...

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:51.520
Yasmin?!

00:17:57.560 --> 00:17:58.640
Midou!

00:17:58.640 --> 00:17:59.390
Tenma!

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:00.140
Tenjin!

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:01.520
No...

00:18:01.990 --> 00:18:04.100
They need proper treatment, and quick!

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:07.220
<i>Can I really cross this wasteland</i>

00:18:07.220 --> 00:18:09.330
<i>without any weapons, supplies, or wheels?</i>

00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:12.260
<i>I'm a traitor with nowhere to go.</i>

00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:14.020
<i>Can I really protect these kids?</i>

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:16.530
Leave us here.

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:17.820
Yasmin?

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:19.990
I don't think we'll make it.

00:18:20.430 --> 00:18:23.030
So leave us and escape, Kotarou...

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:26.500
Rewrite

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:26.500
Don't

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:27.500
Rewrite

00:18:27.880 --> 00:18:28.790
I refuse.

00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:31.890
<i>I see.</i>

00:18:31.890 --> 00:18:35.400
<i>This ability converts my 
life force into power.</i>

00:18:35.750 --> 00:18:37.340
<i>Fine. Take all you want.</i>

00:18:44.090 --> 00:18:46.440
I've decided to live the way I want.

00:18:46.440 --> 00:18:47.840
And live Luis's share, too.

00:18:49.180 --> 00:18:50.450
I promise I'll save you.

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:51.850
Wait for me.

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:56.550
See you, Luis.

00:19:01.560 --> 00:19:03.240
You look awful.

00:19:04.010 --> 00:19:05.840
I apologize for my late return.

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:09.380
I got separated from the others 
due to the carpet bombing.

00:19:09.380 --> 00:19:10.230
Yeah.

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:13.250
You're Team Variant's sole survivor.

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:17.510
Just when we'd wiped out the summoners...

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:19.850
We have plenty of replacements.

00:19:19.850 --> 00:19:23.510
Return to active duty once you sort 
out your team's personal belongings.

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:25.160
Yes, sir.

00:19:26.210 --> 00:19:29.380
<i>Once I decided to stop 
standing still that day,</i>

00:19:29.380 --> 00:19:31.860
<i>a lot of things fell into place.</i>

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:36.130
<i>Even in this country, there was 
a city that was relatively safe.</i>

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:39.370
<i>I gave Yasmin part of my savings</i>

00:19:39.370 --> 00:19:41.550
<i>and had her relocate there with the others.</i>

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:43.780
<i>While they were summoners,</i>

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:47.790
<i>they were only being used 
because they were poor.</i>

00:19:48.180 --> 00:19:51.490
<i>And there were many, many more like them.</i>

00:19:52.550 --> 00:19:53.810
<i>As for me...</i>

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:57.620
<i>I improved after that mission</i>

00:19:57.620 --> 00:20:00.090
<i>and came to be regarded as a solo operator.</i>

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:05.100
<i>I used the freedom that gave me</i>

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:08.510
<i>to take in any summoners I 
found that were being used.</i>

00:20:08.510 --> 00:20:12.150
<i>I also took in superhumans before 
Guardian could find them.</i>

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:15.440
<i>In order to prevent 
Guardian from finding out,</i>

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:17.260
<i>I had to stay away from the place.</i>

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:20.690
<i>But Yasmin and the rest took 
care of everything in my stead.</i>

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:22.820
<i>As a result,</i>

00:20:23.190 --> 00:20:26.700
<i>a group comprised of both summoners 
and superhumans was born.</i>

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:29.560
<i>Simply put, human nature was the reason</i>

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:32.210
<i>Gaia and Guardian were at odds.</i>

00:20:32.590 --> 00:20:36.580
<i>But I felt like that very human nature 
could also allow them to co-exist.</i>

00:20:37.100 --> 00:20:39.120
<i>And nobody could convince me otherwise.</i>

00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:41.090
<i>And then,</i>

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:44.120
<i>around two years after I left Japan,</i>

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:46.260
<i>I got a call from Esaka-san.</i>

00:21:00.770 --> 00:21:03.070
Is that you, Kotarou?

00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:07.890
I just wanted to check on you one last time.

00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:11.160
Are you going back to Japan?

00:21:13.590 --> 00:21:14.540
I see.

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:24.220
Everyone's sad because

00:21:24.890 --> 00:21:27.760
you never come to see us.

00:21:28.150 --> 00:21:30.090
I don't want to cause you any trouble.

00:21:30.090 --> 00:21:32.770
But this is your home.

00:21:33.340 --> 00:21:35.390
Hearing you say that is more than enough.

00:21:35.790 --> 00:21:38.520
All I ever wanted was a 
home, a place to belong.

00:21:38.710 --> 00:21:41.150
Then... Then why?

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:44.860
Of course, I'll keep sending you money.

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:48.380
Though, really, your asset 
management brings in more money

00:21:48.380 --> 00:21:50.410
than I do these days.

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:51.870
That's not it!

00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:52.960
That's not what I...

00:21:52.960 --> 00:21:55.790
That's not what we want!

00:21:56.250 --> 00:21:58.890
There was a beautiful starry sky

00:21:58.890 --> 00:22:01.050
on the night we parted 
with our friends, too.

00:22:02.400 --> 00:22:03.420
Say, Yasmin.

00:22:03.980 --> 00:22:07.100
Have I been able to move 
on without standing still?

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:10.420
I-It's all thanks to you

00:22:10.420 --> 00:22:13.430
that we can live with smiles 
on our faces right now.

00:22:13.720 --> 00:22:15.560
Isn't that enough?

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:17.740
Thank you.

00:22:22.300 --> 00:22:23.480
Kotarou...

00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:25.070
Kotarou!
